@lang en
-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
-- The rules that an enactment, a power and a duty go on from occasion to occasion (s 10, s 22(1), s 23(1)), that a power or duty given to the holder
-- of an office passes to whoever holds it for the time being (s 22(2), s 23(2)), and that the authority that makes rules for a court may make rules
-- for a jurisdiction an enactment confers, extends or varies (s 24). Section 22(3) is in ie-powers-and-service.l4.
--
-- WHAT THESE RULES MEAN FOR A PERSON. A person who relies on an enactment, who holds a power under it, who owes or is owed a duty under it, or who
-- litigates in a court whose jurisdiction an enactment has just changed, can read from these functions: that an earlier use of an enactment, a power or a
-- duty does not exhaust it (s 10, s 22(1), s 23(1)); who may exercise a power and who must perform a duty on a given day (s 22(2), s 23(2)); and
-- which authority may regulate the procedure of the court in that jurisdiction (s 24). The Act does not name who may enforce a duty; the functions do not either.
--
-- JUDGMENTS THE ACT LEAVES TO THE READER ARE INPUTS: whether "occasion requires" an enactment to be applied, a power exercised or a duty performed.
-- "Has ceased to have effect" is an input too; the repeal functions of ie-repeal.l4 are what a caller uses to answer it.
--
-- PRECONDITION, STATED ONCE (section 4(1)): as in the other modules, these functions assume that no contrary intention appears.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

§ `Named refusals`

-- One definition per refusal; each name is its message.

-- src:189 | (2) A power conferred by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be conferred on, and may accordingly be exercised by, the holder for the time being of that office.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 22(2) (src:189)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 22(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who exercises the power when two persons hold the office on the same day` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 22(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who exercises the power when two persons hold the office on the same day"

-- src:192 | (2) A duty imposed by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be imposed on, and shall accordingly be performed by, the holder for the time being of that office.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 23(2) (src:192)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 23(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who performs the duty when two persons hold the office on the same day` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 23(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who performs the duty when two persons hold the office on the same day"

§ `An occasion`

DECLARE `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on` HAS
    `the day of the occasion`                                                   IS A DATE
    `the occasion requires it`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of earlier occasions on which it has already been used`         IS A NUMBER
    `the enactment has ceased to have effect before that day`                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- `the number of earlier occasions on which it has already been used` is read by no rule, on purpose: ss 10, 22(1) and 23(1) say "from time to time",
-- which puts no limit on the number of occasions, so an earlier use never exhausts the enactment, the power or the duty. The tests vary it.
-- `the day of the occasion` is read by no rule either: the sections exclude no day. It is kept so that the record says when the occasion is.

-- src:134 | Enactment always speaking. 10.—An enactment continues to have effect and may be applied from time to time as occasion requires.
-- src:188 | Powers under enactments. 22.—(1) A power conferred by an enactment may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires.
-- src:191 | Duties under enactments. 23.—(1) A duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 10 (src:134); s 22(1) (src:188); s 23(1) (src:191)
GIVEN o IS AN `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the occasion calls on the enactment` o MEANS
        o's `the occasion requires it`
    AND NOT o's `the enactment has ceased to have effect before that day`

§ `Section 10: an enactment continues to have effect and may be applied from time to time as occasion requires`

-- src:134 | Enactment always speaking. 10.—An enactment continues to have effect and may be applied from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 10 (src:134)
GIVEN o IS AN `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an enactment may be applied on the occasion` o MEANS
    `the occasion calls on the enactment` o

§ `Section 22(1): a power conferred by an enactment may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires`

-- src:188 | Powers under enactments. 22.—(1) A power conferred by an enactment may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 22(1) (src:188)
GIVEN o IS AN `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a power conferred by an enactment may be exercised on the occasion` o MEANS
    `the occasion calls on the enactment` o

§ `Section 23(1): a duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires`

-- src:191 | Duties under enactments. 23.—(1) A duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 23(1) (src:191)
GIVEN o IS AN `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a duty imposed by an enactment shall be performed on the occasion` o MEANS
    `the occasion calls on the enactment` o

§ `Sections 22(2) and 23(2): the holder of an office for the time being`

DECLARE `A holder of an office` HAS
    person       IS A STRING
    `first day`  IS A DATE
    `last day`   IS A MAYBE DATE

-- `last day` is the last day on which the person holds the office; NOTHING means the person still holds it.

-- src:189 | (2) A power conferred by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be conferred on, and may accordingly be exercised by, the holder for the time being of that office.
-- src:192 | (2) A duty imposed by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be imposed on, and shall accordingly be performed by, the holder for the time being of that office.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 22(2) (src:189); s 23(2) (src:192)
GIVEN h IS A `A holder of an office`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person holds the office on` h `the day` d MEANS
        h's `first day` AT MOST d
    AND (CONSIDER h's `last day`
         WHEN NOTHING   THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST l    THEN d AT MOST l)

-- Two holders on one day, or none: the functions below say so and do not choose.
-- src:189 | (2) A power conferred by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be conferred on, and may accordingly be exercised by, the holder for the time being of that office.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 22(2) (src:189)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      holders IS A LIST OF `A holder of an office`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the holder for the time being of the office on` d `, the holders being` holders MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN h YIELD `the person holds the office on` h `the day` d) holders
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   null rest
        THEN JUST (x's person)
        ELSE `section 22(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who exercises the power when two persons hold the office on the same day`

-- src:189 | (2) A power conferred by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be conferred on, and may accordingly be exercised by, the holder for the time being of that office.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 22(2) (src:189)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the power is conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      p IS A STRING
      holders IS A LIST OF `A holder of an office`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may exercise the power on` d `, the power being conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` `the power is conferred on the holder of an office as that holder` `, the person being` p `, the holders being` holders MEANS
        `the power is conferred on the holder of an office as that holder`
    AND (CONSIDER `the holder for the time being of the office on` d `, the holders being` holders
         WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST who  THEN who EQUALS p)

-- src:192 | (2) A duty imposed by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be imposed on, and shall accordingly be performed by, the holder for the time being of that office.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 23(2) (src:192)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      holders IS A LIST OF `A holder of an office`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the holder for the time being of the office, for a duty, on` d `, the holders being` holders MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN h YIELD `the person holds the office on` h `the day` d) holders
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   null rest
        THEN JUST (x's person)
        ELSE `section 23(2) speaks of the holder, and does not say who performs the duty when two persons hold the office on the same day`

-- src:192 | (2) A duty imposed by an enactment on the holder of an office as that holder shall be deemed to be imposed on, and shall accordingly be performed by, the holder for the time being of that office.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 23(2) (src:192)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the duty is imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      p IS A STRING
      holders IS A LIST OF `A holder of an office`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person shall perform the duty on` d `, the duty being imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` `the duty is imposed on the holder of an office as that holder` `, the person being` p `, the holders being` holders MEANS
        `the duty is imposed on the holder of an office as that holder`
    AND (CONSIDER `the holder for the time being of the office, for a duty, on` d `, the holders being` holders
         WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST who  THEN who EQUALS p)

§ `Section 24: rules of court for a jurisdiction an enactment confers, extends or varies`

DECLARE `What an enactment does to the jurisdiction of a court` IS ONE OF
    `it confers a new jurisdiction on the court`
    `it extends an existing jurisdiction of the court`
    `it varies an existing jurisdiction of the court`
    `it does none of those things`

-- src:193 | Rules of court. 24.—Where an enactment confers a new jurisdiction on a court or extends or varies an existing jurisdiction of a court, the authority having for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court has, and may at any time exercise, power to make rules or orders for regulating the practice and procedure of that court in the exercise of the jurisdiction so conferred, extended or varied.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 24 (src:193)
GIVEN what IS A `What an enactment does to the jurisdiction of a court`
      `the authority has for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the authority has power to make rules or orders for the practice and procedure of the court in the exercise of the jurisdiction, as conferred, extended or varied` what `the authority has for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court` `, on the day` d MEANS
    CONSIDER what
    WHEN `it confers a new jurisdiction on the court`        THEN `the authority has for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court`
    WHEN `it extends an existing jurisdiction of the court`  THEN `the authority has for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court`
    WHEN `it varies an existing jurisdiction of the court`   THEN `the authority has for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court`
    WHEN `it does none of those things`                      THEN FALSE

-- `d` is read by no rule: s 24 says the authority "may at any time exercise" the power, and excludes no day.
